ula. Situated on the Mediterranean coast, approximately 344 kilometers northeast of Cairo, its strategic location has made it a focal point throughout various historical epochs, especially during the Classical era. The city has roots that trace back to ancient times, playing a significant role in the complex socio-political dynamics of the region, particularly during the reign of various Egyptian dynasties and later during the conflicts involving the Ottoman Empire and British colonial interests.

